SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
Hard register count of the game's retail compiler (notes/COMPILER.md, "Pseudo
register numbers"), for the build psp-gcc-4.0.4a: the LBP-PSP-Decomp kit's
psp-gcc-4.0.4c work tree plus this diff and the other diffs of tools/gcc
(tools/gcc/build_404a.sh). Applies with `patch -p1` in gcc-4.0.4/ after them.
Appends 131 fixed registers, usable in no mode, after the COP3 registers:
FIRST_PSEUDO_REGISTER goes from 176 to 307, so every pseudo register number goes up
by 131. GCSE hashes register numbers (hash_rtx), and the order of its hash buckets
decides which of two equal pseudos global allocation serves first: with 130, 131 or
132 more registers the Bullet sweep goes from 1168 to 1176 of 1695 (with the inline
functions), none lost; any count from 127 to 141 loses none. The number and the
place of the retail registers are not known (the Sony SDK compiler has the
Allegrex's 128 VFPU registers to declare); 131 is the middle of the best range.
GCC code is GPL-2.0-or-later (GCC 4.0.4) and the kit's context GPL-3.0-or-later.
